Name: dkim2_message_instance
Type: ENUM
Allowed-Values: off verify trust
Default-Value: off
Last-Modified: UNRELEASED

Whether a Sieve "redirect" adds a DKIM2 "Message-Instance" header field
documenting the header fields the script changed with "addheader" or
"deleteheader".  Cyrus never signs: the header field is there for whichever
later hop adds the "DKIM2-Signature", and is only added to a message which
already carries a "Message-Instance", since a message outside the DKIM2
chain of custody has nothing to stay attached to.

In "verify" mode the incoming message is hashed and checked against the
highest numbered "Message-Instance" it carries before anything is added,
so that a change made earlier in the delivery pipeline and never declared
cannot be misattributed to this hop.  In "trust" mode that check is
skipped, which is only safe if everything upstream of Sieve is known to
leave signed header fields alone.  In either mode, a message that cannot
be documented honestly is forwarded with no "Message-Instance" added and
the reason logged.
